Tension: let the host own the Vulkan surface (external_surface)
==============================================================

Why this patch exists
---------------------
"Host owns the window. Renderer owns the swapchain."

Ogre-Next can already accept a host-created VkInstance (`external_instance`,
see Samples/2.0/Tutorials/Tutorial_VulkanExternal) and a host-created
VkDevice (`external_device`). What it cannot do is accept a host-created
VkSurfaceKHR: VulkanWindowSwapChainBased::createSurface() is pure virtual and
each backend builds its own surface from a native handle it also created
itself (xcb window, HWND, ANativeWindow). So the renderer always owns the
window, and the window is always the platform's own creation.

That is the blocker for the architecture in INPUT.md: SDL3 creates the window
and the surface (SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN + SDL_Vulkan_CreateSurface, which
implements Wayland, X11 and Win32 WSI in SDL), and Ogre consumes them. Without
this, Ogre binds an X11 window and the app is pinned to XWayland on a Wayland
desktop - the fallback path as the product.

What this patch adds
--------------------
A `miscParams` key `external_surface`: the VkSurfaceKHR as an integer.

  * VulkanWindowSwapChainBased gains mExternalSurfaceKHR and
    adoptExternalSurface(). When the key is present, createSurface() in every
    backend adopts the handle instead of creating one, and the backend does not
    create a native window either (Xcb: no xcb connection or window; Win32: no
    HWND).
  * The handle is borrowed, not owned: destroySurface() drops the reference
    without calling vkDestroySurfaceKHR. The host destroys it, as it does the
    window, the instance and the device.
  * Xcb skips the vkGetPhysicalDeviceXcbPresentationSupportKHR probe when the
    surface is external - there is no xcb connection to pass, and support was
    already settled when the host created the surface.

Absent the key, every path is byte-for-byte what it was: this is additive, and
`createSurface()` still does platform work when no surface was supplied.

Scope, stated so it is not mistaken for more than it is
-------------------------------------------------------
This makes the *renderer* platform-agnostic. It adds no Wayland code to Ogre
and needs none: the WSI lives in SDL, which already implements both Wayland
and X11 correctly. Ogre never learns which one it is running on.

Not verified here: a running external-surface window. Compile-verified against
RenderSystem_Vulkan's own flags; the Win32 translation unit cannot be compiled
on Linux and is unverified. End-to-end proof is the Phase 0/2 spike.

diff --git a/RenderSystems/Vulkan/include/OgreVulkanWindow.h b/RenderSystems/Vulkan/include/OgreVulkanWindow.h
index cd6a764896..e1a536a47c 100644
--- a/RenderSystems/Vulkan/include/OgreVulkanWindow.h
+++ b/RenderSystems/Vulkan/include/OgreVulkanWindow.h
@@ -119,6 +119,11 @@ namespace Ogre
         bool mCanDownloadData;
 
         VkSurfaceKHR mSurfaceKHR;
+        /// Set when the surface was handed to us by the host (params key
+        /// "external_surface"). In that case mSurfaceKHR is a borrowed handle:
+        /// the host created it and the host destroys it, so destroySurface()
+        /// releases our reference without calling vkDestroySurfaceKHR.
+        VkSurfaceKHR mExternalSurfaceKHR;
         VkSwapchainKHR mSwapchain;
         FastArray<VkImage> mSwapchainImages;
         /// Note: We need a semaphore per frame, not per swapchain.
@@ -148,6 +153,12 @@ namespace Ogre
 
         void parseSharedParams( const NameValuePairList *miscParams );
 
+        /// If an external surface was supplied, adopt it as mSurfaceKHR and
+        /// report true so the platform-specific createSurface() can return
+        /// early. False means "make your own", i.e. every path that existed
+        /// before this option.
+        bool adoptExternalSurface();
+
         PixelFormatGpu chooseSurfaceFormat( bool hwGamma );
         virtual void createSurface() = 0;
         virtual void destroySurface();
diff --git a/RenderSystems/Vulkan/src/OgreVulkanWindow.cpp b/RenderSystems/Vulkan/src/OgreVulkanWindow.cpp
index e06b45daf7..b9ded633af 100644
--- a/RenderSystems/Vulkan/src/OgreVulkanWindow.cpp
+++ b/RenderSystems/Vulkan/src/OgreVulkanWindow.cpp
@@ -186,6 +186,7 @@ namespace Ogre
         mClosed( false ),
         mCanDownloadData( false ),
         mSurfaceKHR( 0 ),
+        mExternalSurfaceKHR( 0 ),
         mSwapchain( 0 ),
         mSwapchainSemaphore( 0 ),
         mSwapchainStatus( SwapchainReleased ),
@@ -248,6 +249,20 @@ namespace Ogre
         opt = miscParams->find( "preTransform" );
         if( opt != end )
             mEnablePreTransform = StringConverter::parseBool( opt->second );
+        // A surface the host already created (e.g. SDL_Vulkan_CreateSurface on
+        // the window SDL owns). Value is the VkSurfaceKHR as an integer. The
+        // handle stays the host's: we never destroy it.
+        opt = miscParams->find( "external_surface" );
+        if( opt != end )
+            mExternalSurfaceKHR = (VkSurfaceKHR)StringConverter::parseSizeT( opt->second );
+    }
+    //-------------------------------------------------------------------------
+    bool VulkanWindowSwapChainBased::adoptExternalSurface()
+    {
+        if( !mExternalSurfaceKHR )
+            return false;
+        mSurfaceKHR = mExternalSurfaceKHR;
+        return true;
     }
     //-------------------------------------------------------------------------
     PixelFormatGpu VulkanWindowSwapChainBased::chooseSurfaceFormat( bool hwGamma )
@@ -669,6 +684,13 @@ namespace Ogre
     //-------------------------------------------------------------------------
     void VulkanWindowSwapChainBased::destroySurface()
     {
+        // A borrowed surface belongs to the host that created it. Drop our
+        // reference and leave the handle alive.
+        if( mSurfaceKHR && mSurfaceKHR == mExternalSurfaceKHR )
+        {
+            mSurfaceKHR = 0;
+            return;
+        }
         if( mSurfaceKHR )
         {
             vkDestroySurfaceKHR( mDevice->mInstance->mVkInstance, mSurfaceKHR, 0 );
diff --git a/RenderSystems/Vulkan/src/Windowing/Android/OgreVulkanAndroidWindow.cpp b/RenderSystems/Vulkan/src/Windowing/Android/OgreVulkanAndroidWindow.cpp
index d58aae2d59..350446db96 100644
--- a/RenderSystems/Vulkan/src/Windowing/Android/OgreVulkanAndroidWindow.cpp
+++ b/RenderSystems/Vulkan/src/Windowing/Android/OgreVulkanAndroidWindow.cpp
@@ -397,6 +397,10 @@ namespace Ogre
         if( mDevice->isDeviceLost() )  // notifyDeviceRestored() will call us again
             return;
 
+        // Host-supplied surface takes precedence; see VulkanWindowSwapChainBased.
+        if( adoptExternalSurface() )
+            return;
+
         VkAndroidSurfaceCreateInfoKHR andrSurfCreateInfo;
         makeVkStruct( andrSurfCreateInfo, VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_ANDROID_SURFACE_CREATE_INFO_KHR );
         andrSurfCreateInfo.window = mNativeWindow;
